1
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:26,400
AYUTTHAYA

2
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:04,240
Now, let's move on to the giant
male buffalo milk-tooth division

3
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:07,320
at The Culture of Thai Buffalo.

4
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,520
Our next contestant

5
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:12,480
is number 31, Hom Thong from Boonyod Farm.

6
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,160
His mother is Hom Ngern
from Ayutthaya Province.

7
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,240
HOM THONG - BOONYOD FARM

8
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:20,360
Hom Thong!

9
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,560
HOM THONG, THE TITLE-HUNTING STAR

10
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,120
You can do it, baby!

11
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:40,280
Our next contestant
is the favorite to win this division.

12
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,920
He's already won several competitions.
Number 27,

13
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,720
Racha Uthai from Chok Charoensuk Farm.

14
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,720
He's the son of Suk Charoen
from Uthai Thani Province.

15
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,320
Auem.

16
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,120
Hello, Auem?

17
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,680
Where are you, dear?

18
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,920
Hello, Dad?

19
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,400
Where are you?

20
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,280
At the competition arena?

21
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,160
And where exactly is that, Dad?

22
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:20,640
Uh…

23
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,400
I'm at the Chok Charoensuk Farm booth.

24
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:27,240
Okay, I'll wait here, then.

25
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:35,040
Step right up, folks!
Get your Chok Charoensuk Farm souvenirs.

26
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:38,040
We've got mugs and keychains

27
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,840
and best of all,
T-shirts featuring Racha Uthai.

28
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:44,360
Once they're gone, they're gone.

29
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,360
Here you go.

30
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,520
Wow.

31
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,480
Buffaloes have fan clubs now?

32
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,800
Help! Somebody help! A thief stole my bag!

33
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,840
Catch him! He's got my bag!

34
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:57,760
Help! Somebody catch that thief!

35
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,840
Help!

36
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,080
Catch him! Somebody help!

37
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,360
Hold him! Stay still!

38
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,160
Din!

39
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,480
Auem.

40
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:30,800
Here you go.

41
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,360
-Thank you so much, dear.
-No problem.

42
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,280
Thank you.

43
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,360
Take him away!

44
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,520
Are you okay, Auem?

45
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,680
Who's this little girl?

46
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,840
I can't find my mom.

47
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,000
Can you help me find her?

48
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,200
Excuse me.

49
00:04:58,960 --> 00:04:59,920
Can you see your mom?

50
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:06,360
-See if you can spot your mom.
-Mom! I'm over here!

51
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:09,560
Khaimuk! I'm over here, Khaimuk!

52
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,520
There you go.

53
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,200
Are you okay?

54
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,400
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

55
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,280
Go.

56
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:30,280
So, do you think I'm cool?

57
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,960
No.

58
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:37,680
Hey, I rode a buffalo to catch a thief.
How is that not cool?

59
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:42,600
Here, Dad's blood pressure medication.
Can you give it to him?

60
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,440
Why don't you give it
to Uncle Yod yourself?

61
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:50,640
No way. He'll make me watch
the buffaloes again. I don't feel like it.

62
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,240
Please.

63
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,160
I don't feel like taking it to him either.

64
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,360
You give it to him.

65
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:58,440
-I'm off.
-Din! Wait!

66
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:02,440
Thank you.

67
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,040
-Is that all?
-Yeah.

68
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,720
Okay, you've taken your medicine.
I'm heading back now.

69
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,400
Wait, dear.

70
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,240
You're already here.
Stay and cheer for your little brother.

71
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:19,040
He's made it to the final three.

72
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:19,960
Dad.

73
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:23,360
I have to pack. I'm leaving for Bangkok
early tomorrow morning.

74
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:26,560
You can pack later.
Stay and cheer for your brother first.

75
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,480
Come on.

76
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:33,840
Alright, the results
of the giant male buffalo

77
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,720
milk-tooth division

78
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:38,280
at The Culture of Thai Buffalo

79
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,720
are now in my hands.

80
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:45,760
Let's see who wins.
Will it be number 27, Racha Uthai?

81
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,240
-Racha Uthai!
-Racha Uthai!

82
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,480
Or number 31, Hom Thong?

83
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,120
Hom Thong!

84
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:05,520
But before I announce the winner,
let's hear from our judges.

85
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:09,520
They'll go over each buffalo's strengths
and weaknesses. Please go ahead.

86
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,840
Well, as for Hom Thong,

87
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:14,040
his height is excellent.

88
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:17,200
His leg bones are thick
and well-proportioned.

89
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:21,120
His neck, back,

90
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:24,440
chest, and hindquarters

91
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:28,680
all clearly display
the distinctive traits of a Thai buffalo.

92
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:31,960
His only weakness is his stance.

93
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:36,400
We'd like to see him stand
with his legs a little farther apart.

94
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:39,040
His front legs are too close together.

95
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:42,840
As for Racha Uthai, he's a large buffalo

96
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:45,680
with thick skin,
a beautifully straight back,

97
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:48,120
and a well-proportioned head and horns.

98
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:51,760
However, his leg bones

99
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,400
are a little too slender.

100
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,520
We'd prefer them thicker.

101
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,880
Both are evenly matched
in their strengths and weaknesses.

102
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,400
So, let's reveal the results.

103
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,440
And the judges have decided

104
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,800
that the champion is

105
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,640
number…

106
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,720
31! Hom Thong!

107
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:25,200
We won! Yes!

108
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:26,240
Hom Thong won!

109
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,440
Hom Thong!

110
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,160
Hom Thong!

111
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,559
Hom Thong!

112
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,080
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

113
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:06,120
-Hold on. Stay a little longer.
-What?

114
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,160
Congratulations, Yod.

115
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,680
Hom Thong really is a beauty.

116
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:25,880
No wonder he beat Racha Uthai.

117
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,280
Thank you, sir.

118
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,320
Hom Thong has a bright future.

119
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,200
Sure you won't sell him to me?

120
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,600
I've been after him
since he was in the junior division.

121
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,280
He's really not for sale, sir.

122
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:46,000
Ob loves Hom Thong like a little brother.

123
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,520
What if I offer you more money?

124
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,840
No amount of money could make me sell him.

125
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:02,040
Hom Ngern and Hom Thong
are the only buffaloes we have.

126
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,880
Besides,

127
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,840
I truly love him
like a member of the family.

128
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,760
I'm sorry, sir.

129
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:35,320
How did you raise Racha Uthai
to lose to Hom Thong?

130
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,840
I'm sorry, boss.

131
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:39,920
If Racha Uthai loses again
at the next competition, you're dead!

132
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:41,840
You'd better find a way

133
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,840
to get Hom Thong onto my farm.

134
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,640
Yes, boss.

135
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:59,800
-Hey, Dad, you should've seen it.
-Eat up!

136
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:02,280
-If that buffalo's back hadn't sagged,
-Thank you, dear.

137
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:04,440
I bet he would've won.

138
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,920
-It's all about the balls.
-Hey!

139
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:10,160
-Food's here.
-Here you go.

140
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,160
Dad.

141
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,320
-Thank you.
-Wow!

142
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,360
The school cafeteria's bestsellers.

143
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:18,520
Spicy fried chicken cartilage
and pork with slime sauce.

144
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,040
-Pork with lime sauce!
-Pork with lime sauce!

145
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:22,240
Can I have some first, darling?

146
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,920
-Hey!
-Dad!

147
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:27,120
No chicken cartilage for you.
It'll trigger your gout.

148
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:32,600
Can't have chicken cartilage? No worries.
Here, have this, Dad.

149
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:34,880
No! I'm not Hom Thong!

150
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,920
Sorry, Dad.

151
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,480
My own son's a pest,
and my adopted daughter's so strict.

152
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,400
But my wife's a sweetheart.

153
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,520
-Oh, please!
-Not yet. It's not time for a scolding.

154
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,840
You two are always flirting.

155
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:56,600
How long are you going to celebrate?
You've been at it since this afternoon.

156
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,560
Exactly! I want to make a TikTok video,

157
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:00,880
but I can't.

158
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,040
It's too loud.

159
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:05,040
Come on, Sa-Ing. Your husband Yod

160
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:08,320
worked so hard
to make Hom Thong a champion.

161
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,560
Let him enjoy himself for one day.

162
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,080
That's right, Sa-Ing.

163
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:16,160
We're not just drinking
and having a barbecue.

164
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,160
We're also talking about opening

165
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:21,160
a Thai buffalo conservation center
for the locals.

166
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:24,120
-There you go again!
-That's right.

167
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,520
That's another thing.

168
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:28,800
You've talked about it for years,
but nothing's come of it.

169
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,360
-Honey.
-What?

170
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,560
These things take time.

171
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:40,840
If Phuyai Dech and I pull this off,

172
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,120
the villagers and our children

173
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,240
won't have to leave home
to work in Bangkok.

174
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:46,680
Right, Auem?

175
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,360
Huh?

176
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,240
-Me?
-Yeah.

177
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,920
Dad, you're asking the wrong person.

178
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,720
You should be asking Ob.

179
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,160
I'm asking the right person.

180
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,760
If Phuyai Dech and I succeed,

181
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:01,920
I want you to come back
and manage our conservation center.

182
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:06,600
You graduated from university in Bangkok.
You're well-educated.

183
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:09,520
You could use what you've learned
to help the villagers.

184
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,560
-Let's get back to eating.
-Have some.

185
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:25,240
-Please?
-Okay, I'll have some.

186
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,520
-Skip that for now.
-Grill some for me too.

187
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:41,360
HOM THONG - BOONYOD FARM

188
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,120
Auem, are you asleep?

189
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,240
Coming.

190
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,080
Here.

191
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,920
I'm giving you 5,000 baht
from Hom Thong's prize money.

192
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:09,320
No, Dad. Keep it for yourself.
Why give it to me?

193
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:12,440
I don't need much money living here.

194
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:15,480
But living in Bangkok is expensive.

195
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,960
You said you need new tires
for your car next month. Take it.

196
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:19,520
Dad.

197
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:27,760
Are you trying to bribe me
into coming back to manage the center?

198
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,440
Is it working?

199
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,640
It's just not for me, Dad.
It'd be easier for me

200
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:39,040
to work and send you money
to help open the center.

201
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:42,920
One day, I'll change your mind.

202
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,320
HOM NGERN, QUEEN OF THE FIELDS

203
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:56,800
Get in there.

204
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:00,920
Untie the rope.

205
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:02,720
Hold him.

206
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,000
Come here. This way.

207
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,440
Ow!

208
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:16,560
Why are Hom Ngern and Hom Thong
making such strange noises?

209
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,440
I'll go check on them.

210
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,840
Come here!

211
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:02,680
Come on. This way, hurry.

212
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,680
Hom Thong.

213
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:19,480
Hey! If she wants to follow, take her too.

214
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,000
Go get her!

215
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,400
Come here!

216
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,240
Hurry up.

217
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,560
Hurry.

218
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,400
Hom Thong!

219
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,560
Hom Ngern!

220
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:45,160
Hom Ngern!

221
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:46,960
Hom Thong, my boy!

222
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,600
Hom Ngern!

223
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:51,760
Hom Thong!

224
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,160
Hey, hurry up!

225
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:08,760
Stop! Where are you taking
Hom Ngern and Hom Thong? Stop right there!

226
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,400
Hom Thong!

227
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,839
Let's get out of here.

228
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:44,440
Damn it!

229
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,400
This is bad.

230
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,760
What do we do?

231
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:50,200
What can we do?
See? Hom Thong's gone back.

232
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:53,000
How can we go after him now?
There's been an accident.

233
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,800
Hey, Hom Thong!

234
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,160
Auem!

235
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,360
What?

236
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,720
Have you seen Dad?

237
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:00,920
-He went to check on the buffaloes.
-He's not there.

238
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,040
Neither are Hom Ngern and Hom Thong.

239
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:03,720
-What?
-Yeah.

240
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:07,560
Hurry.

241
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,200
Dad!

242
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,760
Dad!

243
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:15,320
Hom Thong!

244
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:19,120
-Hom Ngern!
-Dad!

245
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,280
Hom Ngern!

246
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,320
Hom Thong! Dad!

247
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,880
-Ob! Any luck?
-No, I can't find Dad anywhere.

248
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,480
I can't find Hom Ngern
or Hom Thong either.

249
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:38,520
Alright, you check the rice fields.
I'll check Aunt Sa-Ang's house.

250
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:41,000
Wait.

251
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:42,880
Hom Thong!

252
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,680
Hom Thong! What are you doing here?

253
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:48,840
Where's Dad?

254
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:53,080
Ob, is that blood?

255
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:56,440
Whoa! It's blood, Auem!

256
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,360
Hom Thong.

257
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:01,880
Hom Thong!

258
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,120
Thank you.

259
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,920
-Dad!
-Dad!

260
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,120
Dad!

261
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:24,240
Dad!

262
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,640
Stay with me, Dad!

263
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:27,720
Is this your father?

264
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,920
I'm so sorry.

265
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,080
I didn't mean to hit him.
I really didn't see him.

266
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:36,600
He suddenly ran after the buffaloes
and right in front of my car.

267
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:38,360
I've already called an ambulance.

268
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,160
Dad.

269
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,160
Dad.

270
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,720
Stay with me.

271
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:58,760
-Dad!
-Dad!

272
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,280
Dad!

273
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:04,160
Dad, wake up!

274
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,880
Dad!

275
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,160
Dad!

276
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:46,560
No! I won't let you leave me, Yod!

277
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:51,600
Mom, please let Dad go.

278
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,600
That's right.

279
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:57,520
Sa-Ing, Yod's at peace now.

280
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,040
If you keep this up,
he'll only worry about you.

281
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:03,680
Good! Then maybe he'll come back to me.

282
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:08,640
Auem.

283
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,240
I'll handle this.

284
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:17,080
How could you leave me like this, Yod?

285
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:21,040
Mom, please calm down.

286
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:24,480
Mom, I know you're hurting.

287
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:26,880
I'm hurting too.

288
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:31,800
But we have to accept
that Dad's no longer with us.

289
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,600
But don't worry, Mom.

290
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:38,080
I'll take care of you, Auem,
and everyone else.

291
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:46,840
Okay?

292
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:51,680
Yod.

293
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,880
Thank you so much, Rut.

294
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:02,360
Don't mention it, Auem.
Your family is like my own.

295
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,960
I'll help you look after everyone now.

296
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:09,200
Don't cry.

297
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:13,080
BOONYOD THADAMIT

298
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:25,240
What are you doing, Ob?

299
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:28,320
Ever since Dad died,
those two have been crying for him.

300
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:31,160
They keep trying to get out
and look for him.

301
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:34,960
Since it's his cremation today,
I brought them to say goodbye.

302
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:39,360
But they're buffaloes, Ob.
How could they understand?

303
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,640
They do.

304
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:48,560
Please, Auem.

305
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:52,520
Let Hom Ngern and Hom Thong
say goodbye to Dad too.

306
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:48,880
How could my dad owe all of you money?

307
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:52,720
Exactly. Why would Yod
borrow money from you?

308
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:54,640
Our family isn't struggling.

309
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:57,920
Here's the loan agreement.
Yod borrowed 500,000 baht from me.

310
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:03,160
He's been paying it back,
but he still owes 320,000.

311
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,360
THE BORROWER AND LENDER
AGREE TO A LOAN OF 500,000 BAHT

312
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,480
And he owes me 450,000.

313
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:12,320
LOAN AGREEMENT UNDER THE NEW CODE

314
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,760
THE BORROWER AGREES TO REPAY THE LOAN
TO THE LENDER BY AUGUST 30

315
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:17,920
But we'll need to verify
these loan agreements first.

316
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,600
I'm not saying anyone's lying.
We just need to be sure.

317
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:22,400
This is a lot of money.

318
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:28,600
Of course. Go ahead and check.
Here are the other loan agreements.

319
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:35,320
Let us know what you decide.
We know you've just cremated your father.

320
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:39,920
But we have bills to pay too.
You understand, don't you?

321
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,200
Auem.

322
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:53,160
Your dad owed the villagers
over a million baht?

323
00:25:57,400 --> 00:26:00,760
Now I know how to get my hands
on Hom Thong.

324
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:12,720
LOAN AGREEMENT UNDER THE NEW CODE

325
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:20,840
How did your dad
get into so much debt, Auem?

326
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:25,280
Auem.

327
00:26:28,840 --> 00:26:31,760
Don't tell me Dad owed you money too.

328
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:33,480
No.

329
00:26:34,520 --> 00:26:36,920
I saw the villagers
asking for their money back.

330
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:40,120
I think I can help you out.

331
00:26:40,760 --> 00:26:42,000
How, sir?

332
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,200
Now that Yod's gone,

333
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:48,280
there's probably no one
to look after Hom Thong.

334
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:51,720
I'd like to buy him
and take care of him myself.

335
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:56,400
But Dad already told you
he wouldn't sell him.

336
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:59,560
Besides, my younger brother
would never agree to it.

337
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,720
But you need money
to pay back the villagers, don't you?

338
00:27:03,440 --> 00:27:06,520
Keeping buffaloes isn't cheap.

339
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:08,320
Your brother's still in school.

340
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:12,440
I think you should cut
whatever expenses you can.

341
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:19,080
Auem, he does have a point.

342
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:28,960
Then let me talk
to my younger brother first.

343
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:32,160
Of course. Talk it over.

344
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,960
Excuse me, sir.

345
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:39,280
How many tens of thousands
would you pay for Hom Thong?

346
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,200
Tens of thousands?

347
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:44,640
Hom Thong's a champion.

348
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:46,520
I'll give you

349
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:48,760
one million baht.

350
00:27:54,760 --> 00:27:56,560
HOM THONG - BOONYOD FARM

351
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:01,280
Yod!

352
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:04,160
Why did you borrow so much money?

353
00:28:04,760 --> 00:28:07,800
Maybe he spent it
on Ob's buffaloes, Mom. Look.

354
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:09,920
Feed, vaccines.

355
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:12,520
And those competitions cost a fortune.

356
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,360
Don't blame my buffaloes!

357
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:17,360
What about your VIP concert tickets?

358
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:20,520
Hey! I only go to a few concerts a year.

359
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:22,640
Dad had to pay for your buffaloes
every single day.

360
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:25,000
So what? My buffaloes help us earn money.

361
00:28:25,080 --> 00:28:26,840
What do you do?

362
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:28,600
All you do is ask Dad for money.

363
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:30,840
-Mom, Ob's picking on me!
-Am I wrong?

364
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:31,960
That's enough!

365
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:35,880
We're all responsible for Dad's debts.

366
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,360
Right now, all Dad has left
in his bank accounts

367
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,680
is just over 30,000 baht.

368
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:46,680
What about Dad's rice fields?

369
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:49,320
The deeds are gone, Mom.
Only the lease agreement is left.

370
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,880
What? Let me see.

371
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:54,240
SALE AND PURCHASE AGREEMENT
OR DEPOSIT AGREEMENT

372
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:58,040
You mean Dad sold the land
and leased it back to farm?

373
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:01,480
So…

374
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:04,520
We've got nothing left?

375
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:08,560
Oh, Yod! Why didn't you
talk to me about any of this?

376
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:12,000
You've left us drowning in debt.
What am I supposed to do now?

377
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:25,920
FIRST PRIZE

378
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:30,800
There's probably no one
to look after Hom Thong.

379
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:34,240
I'd like to buy him
and take care of him myself.

380
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:36,320
I'll give you

381
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:38,440
one million baht.

382
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:28,800
Dad.

383
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:32,680
You owed three million baht?

384
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:36,040
BOONYOD THADAMIT

385
00:30:46,560 --> 00:30:49,040
Hom Ngern, Hom Thong.

386
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:52,080
Dad may be gone,
but I'll take care of you both.

387
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:57,680
Ob.

388
00:30:58,520 --> 00:31:00,120
I need to talk to you.

389
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:04,280
What did Sia Aun say to you yesterday?

390
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,280
He offered to buy Hom Thong.

391
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:14,000
He offered a million baht.

392
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,640
A million?

393
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:17,800
What did you tell him?

394
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:20,680
-I wanted to talk to you first.
-No discussion!

395
00:31:21,320 --> 00:31:23,000
-I'm not selling him.
-Ob.

396
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:25,360
Can you please be reasonable?

397
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:27,760
Those creditors helped Dad
when he had no money.

398
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:30,680
I can't just ignore them.
And we owe three million baht.

399
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:32,400
Even selling my car wouldn't cover it.

400
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:35,040
A million would pay off
a huge chunk of Dad's debt, Ob.

401
00:31:36,360 --> 00:31:37,200
Please.

402
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:39,600
I'm only asking for Hom Thong.

403
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:42,040
Isn't there any other way, Auem?

404
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:45,160
You know how much Dad spent
feeding the buffaloes every month.

405
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:48,360
If we only keep Hom Ngern,
we'll save a lot.

406
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,160
Hom Thong's been with me
since he was born.

407
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:52,480
He's like my little brother. He's family.

408
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:54,240
Then he should do his part for the family.

409
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:57,520
Dad's gone. We all have to help out, Ob.

410
00:31:57,600 --> 00:32:00,960
I'll get a job and earn the money myself.
Please don't sell him.

411
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:03,880
-Hom Thong didn't do anything wrong.
-How can you say that?

412
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:06,760
If he hadn't gotten out that night,

413
00:32:06,840 --> 00:32:09,400
Dad wouldn't have chased him
and gotten hit by a car.

414
00:32:10,040 --> 00:32:11,920
He's the reason Dad died.

415
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:22,560
Is that why you want to sell him?

416
00:32:23,320 --> 00:32:24,760
You hate Hom Thong, don't you?

417
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:35,680
Believe what you want.

418
00:32:38,080 --> 00:32:40,320
I'll have Sia Aun
pick up Hom Thong tomorrow.

419
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:29,800
-Hello, sir.
-Hello.

420
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:32,080
Would you like to come in
for something to drink?

421
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,200
Oh, no need.

422
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,320
Just give me your bank account number.

423
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:38,320
I'll transfer the rest and take Hom Thong.

424
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:49,880
Is something wrong?

425
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:56,160
Well, Ob's hidden Hom Thong somewhere.

426
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:58,600
When Auem and I went outside this morning,

427
00:33:58,680 --> 00:34:00,920
only Hom Ngern was in the pen.

428
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,440
Auem's looking for them,
but hasn't found them yet.

429
00:34:05,760 --> 00:34:07,920
Then I'll have my men help look for them.

430
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,400
-Go!
-Come on, let's go!

431
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:28,840
Hello, Mom. I still can't find Ob.

432
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:33,280
What? Sia Aun's already here,
and he looks pretty upset.

433
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:37,400
Besides the fields behind our house.

434
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:39,719
Where else does Ob
like taking the buffaloes?

435
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:45,719
SAIPHET, THE FARM'S FINEST GEM
TOP-TIER BREEDER DAM

436
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:49,239
PHETKLA, THE PALE PRINCE

437
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:52,960
Saiphet, I've hung
some mineral supplements here.

438
00:34:53,040 --> 00:34:55,920
Eat plenty so you'll grow strong, okay?

439
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:57,720
You're always so stubborn.

440
00:35:02,560 --> 00:35:05,760
Share it between you two, okay?

441
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:12,800
What's that?

442
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:17,280
Hey! Wait!

443
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:20,320
Auem, you just got here
and you're already wandering around.

444
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:22,280
This is a buffalo pen, not Siam Paragon.

445
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:24,920
Did Ob hide Hom Thong here, Din?

446
00:35:25,600 --> 00:35:26,640
Hom Thong's missing?

447
00:35:27,280 --> 00:35:29,520
Yes, and Ob's missing too.

448
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:33,200
You're not hiding something from me
to help Ob, are you?

449
00:35:34,480 --> 00:35:37,560
Auem, I herd buffaloes. I don't cry wolf.

450
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:42,400
Still don't believe me?
Go ahead and search the place.

451
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:05,440
Well…

452
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:08,960
I have to sell Hom Thong
to pay off our debts.

453
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:10,600
But Ob's hidden him somewhere.

454
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:13,560
Do you have any idea
where Ob might have taken him?

455
00:36:13,640 --> 00:36:15,320
You're selling Hom Thong?

456
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:17,120
To whom?

457
00:36:17,200 --> 00:36:18,680
Sia Aun.

458
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:23,000
You're selling Hom Thong to Sia Aun?
Why would you do that?

459
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:25,880
Din, can you please stop asking questions?

460
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:27,880
I know how much Ob loves Hom Thong.

461
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:29,800
But our family owes
almost three million baht.

462
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:32,280
I have to sell whatever I can
to pay it back.

463
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:38,600
Auem!

464
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:42,480
I think I know

465
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:46,320
where Ob might have hidden Hom Thong.

466
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:56,600
Hang in there, okay?

467
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:02,200
Once Sia Aun leaves, I'll take you home.

468
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:18,400
Get out! I'm not selling Hom Thong.

469
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:22,000
Ob, stop being stubborn.

470
00:37:22,080 --> 00:37:23,960
Get Hom Thong into the truck.

471
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:25,880
No!

472
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:27,920
-Don't!
-Hey!

473
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,880
-Don't take Hom Thong!
-Don't hurt him!

474
00:37:32,080 --> 00:37:33,880
-Ob, calm down.
-Ob.

475
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:35,240
Hey.

476
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:36,680
-Take him.
-Ob.

477
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:41,400
Hom Thong.

478
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:48,200
Hey, let go of me.

479
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:49,920
-Hey! Don't!
-Ob!

480
00:38:03,120 --> 00:38:05,120
Oh, Hom Thong.

481
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:13,400
Hey, stop right there!

482
00:38:13,480 --> 00:38:15,840
Ob! Get a hold of yourself!

483
00:38:15,920 --> 00:38:18,080
Give me back Hom Thong.

484
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:22,320
-Calm down, Ob.
-I'm begging you.

485
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:23,520
Let's go.

486
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:26,440
Hom Thong.

487
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:29,160
-Ob.
-Please…

488
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:33,880
-Ob, listen to me.
-Please, let me go.

489
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:36,400
Let go!

490
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,320
-Ob!
-Let me go!

491
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:40,120
Hom Thong.

492
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,720
Hom Thong.

493
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:47,720
Give Hom Thong back.

494
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:57,840
Hom Thong!

495
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:30,960
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
